"Qira felt the waystone flare at dawn, and knows something crossed at the ring."
"Qira has met one outlander before, forty years ago on the coast, and knows the signs."
"Qira would teach a pupil who could feel mana, and has wanted one for twenty years."
"Qira knows the waystone ring and her caves sit on one thread of gray mana under the ridge."
"Qira means to walk to the waystone within days to see what the flare left behind."
